# A fault of a program goes to its fault endpoint (roadmap l4.md L5, L6,
# D18), the OS server's, which the root gave it: the counter faults once
# (TEST_COUNTER_FAULT) while the shell waits for a key; the OS server
# reports it with the module's name, and restarts it; the shell goes on.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_FAULT
keys: {wait 20}echo hi\n
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>rx286: counter fault #UD at 0007:{c:rx_ud2}
echo hi
hi
A:\>
